# What `moon package` / `moon publish` put in the archive.
#
# Publishing honors .gitignore by default, but a .moonignore in the same
# directory replaces it for that whole tree (the two files are not combined),
# so the non-dot-prefixed rules from .gitignore are repeated here. Paths whose
# name begins with `.` are excluded by default at every depth, and the
# package-root `_build/` is always excluded. Git's `.git/info/exclude` and the
# global git ignore configuration are never consulted, so anything that has to
# stay out of a release belongs in this file.

# Local build output — bare `target` matches at every depth, like .gitignore
# does; `/target` would only cover the root and let a nested one ship
target/
target

# Bytecode left by the harness scripts
__pycache__/

# TPC-H fixtures and golden answers — regenerated by harness/gen_tpch.py and
# harness/gen_multigroup.py. They belong in the repository (CI reads them) but
# not in the published module: SF0.1 alone is ~124 MB on disk, which turns the
# archive into ~51 MB of test data.
/harness/data/

# Agent-internal planning documents, also kept out of git
/docs/PLAN.md
/docs/application.md

# Agent workflow guide and local commit hook — dev-side tooling, not part of
# the shipped module (AGENTS.md carries an "agent memory" section)
/AGENTS.md
/hooks/
